select engine_manual_apply(195,'253c3ebd0ba74046600169fcb3f1878c',$p$[{"old": "MiniMax or DeepSeek as either debater (neither debates; DeepSeek is the enforcer, md_notes_rulings 421);", "new": "MiniMax or DeepSeek as either debater (neither debates; md_notes_rulings 421; the enforcer model is luna since ASK 426, §9);"}, {"old": "It always requires the ACTIVE `deepseek` row (the enforcer's model, §9).", "new": "It always requires the ACTIVE `deepseek` row (the `deepseek` seat's own calls) and, since ASK 426, the ACTIVE `luna` row (the enforcer model, RS.enforcer, §9)."}, {"old": "DeepSeek is called on its own endpoint, only as the enforcer (§9).", "new": "The `deepseek` seat is called on its own endpoint (api.deepseek.com); the enforcer model, luna since ASK 426, is called through OpenRouter (§9)."}, {"old": "the enforcer call sends the `deepseek` row's max_tokens, at least 16,000.", "new": "the enforcer call sends the enforcer row's max_tokens (RS.enforcer, the `luna` row since ASK 426), at least 16,000."}, {"old": "- THE SECOND READING (DeepSeek, ruling 428): after the cure, Judge Enforcer Build sends every panel judge's lines to the `deepseek` model", "new": "- THE SECOND READING (the enforcer model, ruling 428): after the cure, Judge Enforcer Build sends every panel judge's lines to the enforcer model (RS.enforcer; luna since ASK 426)"}, {"old": "One call to the `deepseek` model checks every panel judge's K-W and K-S3 answer.", "new": "One call to the enforcer model (RS.enforcer; luna since ASK 426) reads every panel judge's K-W and K-S3 answer."}, {"old": "DeepSeek is the enforcer (§9).", "new": "the enforcer model is luna since ASK 426 (§9)."}, {"old": "(or deepseek for the enforcer)", "new": "(or deepseek for the `deepseek` seat)"}, {"old": "  - THE OPENING VERDICT WORD OF A RECOMPUTED JUDGMENT IS REPLACED (pkgRHD, ASK 297; Alternate Merge):", "new": "  - THE ENFORCER MODEL IS LUNA (ASK 426; Resolve Seats; Enforcer Build, Anticheat Build, Close Enforcer Build, Judge Contradiction Build and Assume Check Build; one Shared Library line read by Judge Enforcer Build, Alt Judge Enforcer Build and R2 Alt Judge Enforcer Build, engine and child; 13 engine and 4 child enforcer HTTP nodes):\n    - Why: the operator chose luna (openai/gpt-6-luna) to replace deepseek-flash as the enforcer model. On the ASK 410 test (49 stored prompts, each sent twice, scored against agreed gold labels), luna read 14 facts STATED that the gold reads NOT STATED, against deepseek-flash's 21; its errors against the gold were 37 against 42, and its unreadable lines 0.8 percent against 6.3.\n    - What it does: Resolve Seats adds RS.enforcer = {seat luna, api_model, max_tokens} from the active `luna` model_config row; a run is refused if that row is missing. The line that picks the enforcer model, in each of the five builds and in the one Shared Library line, reads RS.enforcer instead of RS.deepseek. The 17 enforcer HTTP nodes post to openrouter.ai with the OpenRouter credential instead of api.deepseek.com. The request is otherwise the same: the same prompts, temperatures and max_tokens rule (the larger of the row value and 16,000, or 8,000; 64,000 on both rows), and no reasoning or effort field. Every record node reads choices[0].message.content as before.\n    - Not changed: every prompt, code check and record node; the 24 other HTTP nodes that call the `deepseek` seat (synthesis, independent verdict, diagnostic, the round calls and their B and G calls, Panel Reserve, the Panel Judge 1 retry, Accept and Accept Return). Node names keep the word \"deepseek\", because renaming them would break the $() references.\n    - Luna as a judge: luna is in neither ORDER0 nor __ALT, so it cannot be seated as judge or alternate. If it is put back in either list, it would enforce its own replies.\n    - Shown offline: the request bodies cut from the built Assume Check Build (E-ASSUME) and from the library's Judge Enforcer Build (E-ANS) equal the bodies sent in the luna test. Not shown: Close Enforcer and Judge Contradiction also send a second copy at temperature 0.6, which the test did not send.\n    - Live: engine b780b2ae (from 1861543f), saved 02:17:21Z on 11-19; child 7b043bab (from c226d9cb), saved 02:17:27Z on 11-19; lib_sha c91b9f1489e9c132 on both.\n    - Limits: not shown by a run; its mark is judge_model \"openai/gpt-6-luna\" on every debate_enforcer_log row of kind enforcer_check, and none deepseek-flash.\n  - THE OPENING VERDICT WORD OF A RECOMPUTED JUDGMENT IS REPLACED (pkgRHD, ASK 297; Alternate Merge):"}, {"old": "The DeepSeek enforcer calls are split", "new": "The enforcer model's calls are split"}, {"old": "A DeepSeek enforcer retry half", "new": "An enforcer retry half"}, {"old": "The DeepSeek enforcer's E-SYN item", "new": "The enforcer model's E-SYN item"}, {"old": "the DeepSeek enforcer calls are split and resent once (§9)", "new": "the enforcer model's calls are split and resent once (§9)"}]$p$::jsonb,null,null,null,null,null,false) r;